### Additional Context

I think it's a bug, becouse if i do similar in pydantic model myself it will work
```python
from typing import Annotated

from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
from pydantic.json_schema import SkipJsonSchema


class A(BaseModel):
    a: Annotated[
        dict[int, int] | SkipJsonSchema[None],
        Field(json_schema_extra={"default": {1: 1}})
    ] = None


import json
print(json.dumps(A.model_json_schema(), indent=4))
```
```
{
    "properties": {
        "a": {
            "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "integer"
            },
            "default": {
                "1": 1
            },
            "title": "A",
            "type": "object"
        }
    },
    "title": "A",
    "type": "object"
}
```
It feels like a leaky abstraction between the function definition and the Pydantic model.

